From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: geni-qcom: leave successful GPI messages in progress

The SPI core owns successful transfer accounting and stops processing when
msg->status changes from -EINPROGRESS. Setting zero in the GPI callback skips
actual_length accounting and any subsequent transfer. Keep successful messages
in progress; DMA errors and residue still set -EIO before completion.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -383,17 +383,17 @@
 {
 	struct spi_controller *spi = cb;
 
-	spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
 	if (result->result != DMA_TRANS_NOERROR) {
+		spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
 		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA txn failed: %d\n", result->result);
 		spi_finalize_current_transfer(spi);
 		return;
 	}
 
 	if (!result->residue) {
-		spi->cur_msg->status = 0;
 		dev_dbg(&spi->dev, "DMA txn completed\n");
 	} else {
+		spi->cur_msg->status = -EIO;
 		dev_err(&spi->dev, "DMA xfer has pending: %d\n", result->residue);
 	}
 
